AC-1: real AES-256-GCM roundtrip preserves exact SQLite feedback with private temporary modes and ciphertext-only padded envelope
AC-2: wrong key, altered ciphertext, duplicate fields, truncation and foreign repository/channel/key bindings fail before opening plaintext SQLite
AC-3: unchanged state avoids nonce/checkpoint churn; lost-ack replay starts from authoritative ciphertext and preserves idempotent records
AC-4: failed intake, invalid key/database and foreign SQLite identity cannot publish partial state; private plaintext is removed after success or failure
